lines=['Built slice 6: exceptions-21-main, inherit-guards, feature-set-link-main and lint-features, preserving main slice 2.',f'Branch compiler/loom-r-slice-6; one commit on {base}; full delivery SHA is in the push receipt and final response.','Commands/results: bounded four-CPU package runs, Linux clang 20.1.8 counts regeneration, guards, formatting, vet and a-check are itemized below.','Mutants: every attempted mutation, catcher and observed status is itemized below; raw failures are retained.', 'Not fully green or Loom-ready: broad stage1 readers hit memory exhaustion; over-budget and incomplete coverage is listed below.','','## Extraction and assumptions','',f'Base: `{base}`. Source: `26f45b7f2029fae240b0d216ea6ecb477e835efa` on `55347dce1537c0bd05d35eab0dc5d663c4823803`. Method: `git merge-tree --write-tree --merge-base=55347dce15 origin/main 26f45b7f20`, then apply the returned tree and resolve. This retains main infrastructure rather than replaying the old main merge as a reverse diff. Source review and runtime conditions are preserved in review/compiler/chain-slices/slice-6.md and review/compiler/chain-slice-6/.','', 'Conservative choices: keep main async support, OrdinaryToPrimitive semantics, lexical readiness, portable cache recipes and strict WASI product infrastructure. Pending exception payload may be NULL for undefined; both payload and pending bit stay thread-local. Parallel propagation selects by exception_index under the existing scheduler lock and restores both words around helping. New Error-name literals are immutable, not shared mutable state. Main runtime statics registry lists the new TLS and immortals. Runtime clearance is still required for the full diff below, including union.c and the adapted main consumers.','', 'Runtime condition: exactly one line, `Uncaught Name: message` for actual Error instances, otherwise `Uncaught ` plus undefined/null/number/boolean/string/function/object. Escape CR/LF, replace lone surrogates, flush stdout and stderr, release payload, exit 1. JS writes the same bytes synchronously; no Node stack.','', 'Setup: GOPROXY=https://proxy.golang.org|direct. nproc=5, cgroup four CPUs; GOMAXPROCS=4 and test runner affinity restricted to four CPUs. House Go 1.27.1, Node 24.19.0 and clang 20.1.8. setup.sh hit timeout 300 (exit 124) during cold Go warming after successful submodule clone: go 0.039s, node 0.023s, markdown 0.090s, clang 0.245s, submodules 257.237s, shared-cache-off 257.239s. No final setup timing. Sourced its provisioned environment and completed required builds directly. An initial reference clone rejected a shallow reference; normal setup clone succeeded. Cache/product relocation, byte-verified archive deduplication and WASI SDK 27 installation addressed disk pressure; no cohere code was copied into Adamic.','','## Conflicts','']
